  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_042 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.715 acc. We have strong evidence that multiprofile >> singleprofile and multimodal > RNA-only, and that scvi_n200 >> scgpt. However, the only aggregation method tested in multiprofile settings is avgpool. Uncertainty: It is unknown whether a transformer-based aggregation could better model inter-profile interactions than simple averaging, potentially unlocking further gains on top of the already-strong config_042. Question tested: config_048 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other variables (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion, multiprofile) identical to config_042, giving a clean A/B comparison of aggregation strategy. Why best next experiment: It is the most informative single-variable extension of the current best, directly isolating the effect of aggregation—a core design axis for multiprofile models—without confounding other choices. If transformer aggregation helps, it identifies a new productive direction; if not, it confirms avgpool sufficiency and redirects budget toward fusion or encoder choices."
}

